.TH QIBOCAL 1 "October 2, 2026" "qibocal-report" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
qibocal \- serve calibration reports and dispatch interactive notebooks
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B qibocal
.RB [ \-\-version ]
.RB [ \-\-help ]
.I COMMAND
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
qibocal-report provides the qibocal command for report servers, local
configuration management, and notebook sessions. Use
.B qibocal COMMAND \-\-help
for the available command options.
.SH NOTEBOOK
.B qibocal notebook connect
.RI [ CONNECTION ]
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.PP
Start JupyterLab (default) or Marimo and open its authenticated URL in the
local browser. Keep the command running for the lifetime of the session.
Ctrl+C stops the notebook, releases its SLURM allocation,
and closes the tunnels.
.PP
The connection layers compose:
local machine, optional SSH access node, optional SLURM computing node.
Omitting SSH submits from the local machine. Omitting SLURM runs on the access
node. Omitting both starts a local notebook.
.PP
Each worker immediately logs its node identity to standard error:
actual hostname, fully qualified domain name, user, OS release, architecture,
Python executable and version, process ID, and working directory on arrival.
SLURM sessions distinguish access and compute nodes and include available
allocation details: cluster, job and step IDs, partition, node lists,
CPU and memory allocation, and GPU IDs.
Without SLURM, one node serves both access and compute roles.
.PP
Node details appear in labeled Rich panels, with colored startup stages
and a ready banner. All formatting happens locally; remote workers forward
structured diagnostics without requiring Rich or a terminal on SSH or SLURM
nodes. Redirected output has no automatic ANSI colors.
Diagnostics remain on standard error and the authenticated URL remains
on its own line on standard output.
.SS Connect options
.TP
.BI \-\-ssh " TEXT"
SSH options followed by a host or user@host destination.
Quote the entire value when including options, for example
.BR "\-\-ssh '\-p 2222 \-i ~/.ssh/lab user@login'" .
Host aliases, agent authentication, and jump hosts from SSH configuration work.
The destination must be the last argument; do not include a remote command.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-queue " " \fIPARTITION\fR
SLURM partition passed to srun on the access node.
.TP
.BI \-\-slurm " TEXT"
Additional srun options as a quoted argument string, for example
.BR "\-\-slurm '\-\-time=02:00:00 \-\-account=lab \-\-gres=gpu:1'" .
Specifying this option alone also enables SLURM dispatch.
Resource allocation must select one task on one computing node.
Only common scheduling/resource options are accepted; command, IO,
and working-directory overrides are rejected. Use separated short options
(for example, \-c 2 rather than \-c2).
.TP
.BR \-w ", " \-\-workdir " " \fIDIRECTORY\fR
Change directory on the access node before starting the session or submitting
to SLURM. With SLURM, this directory must also be accessible on the computing
node. Relative kernel paths are resolved in the notebook working directory.
.TP
.B \-\-marimo
Run Marimo instead of JupyterLab.
.TP
.B \-\-jupyter
Use JupyterLab, including when overriding a named Marimo connection.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-no\-interactive
Print the authenticated URL without opening a browser. The command still
stays attached to supervise the notebook and tunnels.
.TP
.B \-\-interactive
Open the browser, including when overriding a named non-interactive connection.
.TP
.BI \-\-venv " NAME_OR_PATH"
Kernel environment on the computing node; default:
.BR qibocal .
Names resolve under
.BR $XDG_CACHE_HOME/qibocal/envs/
(fallback:
.BR ~/.cache/qibocal/envs/ ).
Absolute paths and explicit relative paths (./env or ../env) are used directly.
Existing environments are never overwritten. Jupyter leaves target environments
unchanged; with \-\-marimo, Marimo is installed directly into the target environment.
When the default named environment qibocal is missing, it is created with
the latest public Qibocal release using pip install qibocal.
You can replace it with a development version or manage its dependencies
afterward. Other missing kernel environments are created with pip but no
calibration packages; install your calibration dependencies into them separately.
.TP
.BI \-\-timeout " SECONDS"
Maximum startup time, including environment preparation, queue wait, and
tunnel setup. Default: 300. Increase this for long SLURM queue waits.
.TP
.BI \-\-subnet " CIDR"
Restrict SLURM computing-node IP selection to an IPv4 or IPv6 subnet,
for example 192.168.0.0/24. Among matching addresses, choose the IP with the
longest network prefix in common with an access-node IP.
Startup fails if no usable computing-node IP matches.
Local and unscheduled SSH sessions still bind only to loopback.
.SS Requirements and environments
Local execution requires Python 3.10+ with venv support. SSH execution requires
OpenSSH locally and python3 (3.10+) with venv support on the access
and computing nodes. SLURM execution requires srun on the access node
and network access from the access node to the allocated computing node.
Both nodes need hostname \-I to report their interface addresses.
The launcher selects a computing-node IP by the longest common network prefix
with an access-node address; hostname resolution and SSH access to the computing
node are not required.
Address discovery and the notebook run in the same single SLURM allocation.
Local and unscheduled SSH notebook servers bind only to loopback.
SLURM notebook servers bind to the selected computing-node interface, not all
interfaces, and are protected by a generated authentication token.
The access worker relays its loopback port to that interface; SSH sessions
tunnel access-node loopback to the local machine. The access-to-compute network
hop is not encrypted, so use SLURM notebooks only on a trusted computing network.
Every session uses a generated authentication token.
.PP
Jupyter server dependencies are installed on first use into the separate managed
jupyter environment under $XDG_CACHE_HOME/qibocal/envs/
(fallback: ~/.cache/qibocal/envs/), not the kernel environment.
Marimo is installed directly into the target environment and launched with its
Python; no separate Marimo environment is used. Installing notebook dependencies or
Qibocal into a new default kernel requires package-index access
on the computing node and either ensurepip or pip (22.3+) in the worker's Python.
All newly created environments include pip. If ensurepip is unavailable,
the worker uses the external installer to install pip and any requested
dependencies into the new environment; system packages
are not changed. This requires package-index access even for otherwise empty
kernel environments. Existing Jupyter server environments are reused as-is.
If first-time installation fails, repair that server environment explicitly
using the command reported by the launcher; it is never implicitly overwritten.
Jupyter exposes the selected environment as the default kernel named
.BR Qibocal .
Its kernel uses that environment's Python and packages, with server-provided
ipykernel dependencies as a fallback.
This keeps an existing Jupyter calibration environment unchanged; server dependencies
may still appear in the notebook's import path.
.SS Named connections
Create a JSON object whose keys are connection names and values are options:
.PP
.nf
{
  "mychip": {
    "ssh": "myuser@login",
    "queue": "mychip",
    "workdir": "/shared/calibration",
    "venv": "qibocal",
    "slurm": "--time=02:00:00",
    "marimo": false,
    "no_interactive": false,
    "timeout": 900
  }
}
.fi
.PP
Save it to
.BR $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/qibocal/notebooks.json ,
with
.BR ~/.config/qibocal/notebooks.json
as the fallback. QIBOCAL_REPORT_CONFIG_DIR overrides its containing directory.
Invoke
.BR "qibocal notebook connect mychip" .
Explicit command-line options override the connection's values.
Unknown options, invalid types, missing names, and malformed files are errors.
The connect command does not create or modify the connection file.
.SS Adding connections
.B qibocal notebook add
.RI [ CONNECTION ]
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.PP
With no options, prompt first for the connection name if not supplied, then show a
multiple-selection menu of options to change from their defaults, then ask for
each selected value. Unselected options retain their defaults.
.PP
To register a connection without the setup menu, provide its name and options
together. The options are identical to those of
.BR "qibocal notebook connect" ;
see Connect options above or
.BR "qibocal notebook connect \-\-help" .
If options are provided without a name, prompt only for the name.
A name alone opens the setup menu for that connection.
Explicitly supplied options are saved in their JSON configuration representation.
Other connections are preserved; an existing name is an error.
Adding a connection does not start a notebook session.
.SS Listing connections
.B qibocal notebook list
.RB [ \-\-raw ]
.PP
Display registered names and their configured options in a Rich table.
An empty registry is reported without creating a file.
With \-\-raw, print the connection file verbatim, without formatting or JSON
validation; a missing file is an error.
.SS Updating connections
.B qibocal notebook update
.RI [ CONNECTION ]
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.PP
Update an existing connection using the same options as connect.
Explicitly supplied settings replace their stored values; unspecified settings
and other connections are preserved. With no options, show the option-selection
menu using the connection's current values. Prompt for the name if omitted.
Missing connections and invalid resulting options are errors.
Updating a connection does not start or stop a notebook session.
.SS Removing connections
.B qibocal notebook remove
.I CONNECTION
.PP
Remove the named connection immediately, without confirmation.
The name must exist. Other connections, environments, and running sessions
are unchanged. Removing the last connection leaves an empty JSON object.
.SS Examples
.nf
qibocal notebook connect
qibocal notebook connect --venv ./calibration-env --marimo
qibocal notebook connect --ssh myuser@login --workdir /shared/runs
qibocal notebook connect --queue mychip --no-interactive
qibocal notebook connect --ssh myuser@login -q mychip --timeout 900
qibocal notebook connect mychip --jupyter -n
qibocal notebook add
qibocal notebook add mychip --ssh myuser@login -q mychip
qibocal notebook list
qibocal notebook list --raw
qibocal notebook update mychip --subnet 192.168.0.0/24
qibocal notebook remove mychip
.fi
.SH REPORT COMMANDS
.TP
.BR "qibocal report server" " [DIRECTORY]"
Serve reports and the embedded web app. Directory defaults to the current
directory. Options: \-\-host (localhost), \-\-port (8000), \-\-auth/\-\-no-auth.
.TP
.B qibocal report client
Serve the standalone report client. Options: \-\-host (127.0.0.1),
\-\-port (8000), \-\-reload.
.TP
.BR "qibocal report dev" " [DIRECTORY]"
Run backend and Vite development servers. Options: \-\-host (localhost),
\-\-port (8000), \-\-frontend-port (5173), \-\-reload/\-\-no-reload,
\-\-auth/\-\-no-auth. Requires the frontend sources and Node.js.
.TP
.BR "qibocal report export" " [OUTPUT_DIR]"
Export the static report client (default: ./dist).
Options: \-\-build/\-\-no-build and \-\-base-path.
.TP
.B qibocal report admin list
List administrators. Options: \-\-all (include all users), \-\-json.
.TP
.BR "qibocal report admin invite" " [USERNAME]"
Generate an administrator invitation. Options: \-u/\-\-username,
\-\-server-url, \-\-host, \-\-port, \-e/\-\-expires-in-hours,
\-\-interactive/\-\-no-interactive, \-\-json.
.BR "qibocal report invite"
is an equivalent shortcut.
.SH CONFIG COMMANDS
.TP
.B qibocal config path
Print the absolute report configuration directory without creating it.
.TP
.B qibocal config clean
Ask before removing servers.json and authentication data.
\-f/\-\-force skips confirmation. Does not remove notebooks.json, notebook
environments, reports, unrelated files, or directories.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Configuration root for notebook connections.
.TP
.B XDG_CACHE_HOME
Cache root for computing-node kernel and notebook server environments.
Each node uses its own value; the local value is not forwarded over SSH.
.TP
.B XDG_RUNTIME_DIR
Location for temporary notebook kernel specifications on the computing node.
When unset, empty, or pointing to a missing directory, use the system temporary
directory. A missing directory is reported in the startup diagnostics.
.TP
.B QIBOCAL_REPORT_CONFIG_DIR
Override the local report and notebook connection configuration directory.
.TP
.B QIBOCAL_AUTH_FILE
Override the report authentication database.
.TP
.B QIBOCAL_REPORT_DIR
Report directory used by the report server.
.TP
.B QIBOCAL_FRONTEND_URL
Frontend development-server URL.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero on normal completion or an orderly notebook Ctrl+C shutdown.
Nonzero on invalid configuration, startup failure, timeout, or session failure.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ssh (1),
.BR srun (1),
.BR python3 (1)
